## Authority Chain

Every KB built on these rules has a strict artifact authority hierarchy. Lower-tier artifacts must never contradict higher-tier ones.

| Tier | Artifact Type | Authority |
|------|---------------|-----------|
| 0 (highest) | Business Requirements (BR) | Defines what the system must accomplish. All other artifacts must be traceable to a BR. |
| 1 | ADR | Defines what was decided and why. Must be traceable to a BR. All other artifacts must reflect ADR decisions. |
| 2 | ARCH | Describes how the system works. Must be consistent with ADRs. Contains no decisions. |
| 3 | Spec Design (design.md) | Describes how something is built. Must be consistent with ADRs and ARCH artifacts. |
| 4 | Runbook (RBK) | Operational procedures. Must implement what BRs, ADRs, ARCH, and spec designs specify. |
| 5 | Wiki | Narrative summaries and Confluence-ready pages. Follow DOCS PREFLIGHT when updating. |

Scratch files are explicitly exempt from all consistency rules. They are working notes and are never authoritative, even if they contradict a higher-tier artifact.

