### ARCH — Architecture Artifacts

Location: `Archs/ARCH-NNN-Short-Title.md`

```
# ARCH-NNN: Full Title

## Date
YYYY-MM-DD

## Purpose
One paragraph. What this artifact describes and what it does not cover.

## [Descriptive sections]
Named by topic. Use ## for top-level sections, ### for subsections.
Tables and bullet lists preferred over prose where structure helps.
```

Rules:
- No Status section. ARCH artifacts are always current descriptions of the system.
- No decisions. ARCH artifacts describe. ADRs decide.
- Date and Purpose are always the first two sections.
- If a Constraints or Risks section is relevant, include it. Risks table uses the same four-column format as ADRs.

