## Confluence Integration

Confluence is a constant in Paul's KBs. The following rules apply to all Confluence publishing.

### Critical Facts

- All Confluence pages are published using `content_format: storage` (Confluence XHTML). This is NOT Markdown publishing.
- Publishing with `content_format: markdown` will destroy all rich formatting (status badges, colored panels, styled tables). Never do this for pages that already exist with storage format content.
- The `index.md` files in `Wiki/` are NOT directly publishable. They are the KB source. The publishable content is storage format XHTML constructed from the Markdown source.
- Always use MCP tools (`mcp_mcp_atlassian_confluence_*`) for Confluence operations. Never use shell scripts.

### Workflow: Creating a New Page

1. Draft content in the Wiki/ Markdown file.
2. Construct Confluence storage format (XHTML) with appropriate macros.
3. Call `create_page` with `content_format: storage`.

### Workflow: Updating an Existing Page

1. Call `get_page` with `convert_to_markdown: false` to get raw storage format.
2. Modify the storage format XHTML directly. Do NOT convert to Markdown and back.
3. Call `update_page` with `content_format: storage` and the full page body.

### Page Ownership Model

**KB-Managed pages** — KB is source of truth. Direct Confluence edits will be overwritten on next publish. Publishing flow: edit .md → construct XHTML → publish.

**Team-Owned pages** — Confluence is source of truth for current content. Team members may edit directly. Publishing flow: get live content → modify XHTML → publish → update .md to match.

**Confluence-Managed pages** — Confluence is sole source of truth. KB holds a read-only snapshot. Never publish, update, or overwrite these pages via MCP tools. If asked to publish one, refuse and explain.

### Storage Format Quick Reference

Status badge:
```xml
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="status" ac:schema-version="1">
  <ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter>
  <ac:parameter ac:name="title">LABEL</ac:parameter>
</ac:structured-macro>
```
Available colours: Green, Yellow, Blue, Red, Grey

Panel:
```xml
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="panel" ac:schema-version="1">
  <ac:parameter ac:name="borderColor">#0052CC</ac:parameter>
  <ac:parameter ac:name="bgColor">#DEEBFF</ac:parameter>
  <ac:parameter ac:name="title">TITLE</ac:parameter>
  <ac:rich-text-body><p>Content</p></ac:rich-text-body>
</ac:structured-macro>
```

Warning box:
```xml
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning" ac:schema-version="1">
  <ac:rich-text-body><p>Warning text</p></ac:rich-text-body>
</ac:structured-macro>
```

