## Open Work Tracking

Every KB using these rules maintains a `current-work-status.md` file (or equivalent). This file is the live state record. It contains:

- Active initiatives with progress and next steps
- Frozen/deferred initiatives
- Open incidents
- In-flight specs
- Pending decisions
- Deferred Items (the parking lot for scope expansions)

The `status` and `what` commands read this file. Keep it current. Completed work is removed; it does not accumulate here.

### Deferred Items

The Deferred Items section is the stopping rule's parking lot. When scope expansion is detected and Paul chooses to park it, it goes here with:
- A one-line description of the topic
- Why it appeared (what sparked the expansion)
- Whether it has a dependency on current work

Deferred Items are not failures. They are evidence that Paul has named an implication without obligating himself to act on it immediately.
